# AIDOCS local MCP config (contains absolute paths)
.mcp.json

# Build / cache / runtime trash — never source, never shipped. Keep the tree
# clean so the deploy gate's committed-tree scan stays lean + deterministic
# (these were the bloat behind the 2026-06-01 trufflehog scan-abort).
.ruff_cache/
.basedpyright/
.pytest_cache/
.pytest-tmp/
.pytest-aidocs-global-config/
.pytest-out-*.log
dist/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
# transient license-patch scratch (applied; not part of the package)
PYPROJECT_LICENSE_SNIPPET.toml
pyproject.toml.license.patch

# mcp/scratch — 612 MiB of working artefacts that NOTHING was ignoring (#912).
#
# WHY THE ROOT RULES DID NOT COVER THIS. The repo-root .gitignore carries
# `/scratch/_*` and `/scratch/probe_*`, but a LEADING SLASH anchors a pattern to
# the directory holding the .gitignore — so those rules cover the repo-root
# `scratch/` tree and have never reached `mcp/scratch/`. Two scratch trees, one
# set of rules, and the gap was invisible because both are called scratch.
# Measured 2026-08-25: `git check-ignore` matched exactly ONE rule anywhere in
# this tree (`__pycache__/`), leaving 337 of 388 files untracked-but-not-ignored,
# among them a 581 MB mutation_coverage_map.json.
#
# THIS HAS ALREADY FIRED ONCE. mcp/scratch/COMMITMSG_lint_isc.txt:42-43 records
# an earlier `git add -A mcp/scratch` that swept 317 files / 577k insertions and
# had to be reset. One `git add -A` from any agent or any human repeats it, and
# the blast radius has only grown since.
#
# IGNORING IS SAFE FOR THE LOAD-BEARING FILES, and this is the part worth being
# explicit about rather than trusting to memory. Five artefacts here ARE
# load-bearing — mutation_pilot.py:842-850 and scripts/deploy_aidocs_gate.sh:
# 4850-4857 name them literally, the gate scp's them back from the VPS, and
# `--report` reads them. `.mutation_inflight/` additionally holds UN-MUTATED
# PRODUCTION SOURCE while a mutation run is in flight (mutation_pilot.py:858-871).
# None of that is harmed here: every one of those paths is read FROM DISK, never
# from git, and a .gitignore rule has NO EFFECT on a file that is already
# tracked. So this stops accidental mass-staging without touching what the
# mutation lane and the deploy gate actually consume.
#
# It is also a blind spot by COMBINATION rather than by bug:
# runtime_provisioner.py:157 deliberately excludes mcp/scratch from source-drift
# detection (correct — it is a scratch dir), and git was ignoring none of it. A
# directory that is neither watched nor ignored is exactly where 581 MB
# accumulates unnoticed.
# EXCEPT the gate proofs (#1022, 2026-09-04). A proof harness whose result is
# only ever agent-reported from a temp path is not evidence anyone can check;
# these two files are small, hand-written and meant to be re-run by a reader.
#
# THE PATTERN IS `scratch/*`, NOT `scratch/`, AND THAT DIFFERENCE IS THE WHOLE
# TRICK. git does not descend into an EXCLUDED DIRECTORY, so under a bare
# `scratch/` no `!` rule beneath it can ever re-include anything -- measured
# here: `git check-ignore -v` still reported `scratch/` for both files. Matching
# the ENTRIES instead leaves the directory itself considered, so the negation
# below is reachable. Everything else under scratch/ stays ignored exactly as
# before (an ignored directory's contents are ignored recursively).
scratch/*
!scratch/gate-proofs/
